{"hw":"καίπερ","html":"<div class=\"lex-entry\"><h4 class=\"lex-hw gk\">καίπερ</h4><span class=\"lex-orth gk\">καίπερ</span>, in <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Hom.</span> </span> always with a word between (exc.<div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"1\"><span class=\"lex-n\">A</span> <span class=\"gk\">καί περ πολλὰ παθόντα</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Od.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">7.224</span> </span> ); but one word in <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pi.</span> </span> and Prose, and usu. in Trag. </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"2\"><span class=\"lex-n\">I</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">even</b>, <span class=\"gk\">καὶ αὐτοί περ πονεώμεθα</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Il.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">10.70</span> </span>. </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"2\"><span class=\"lex-n\">II</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">although, albeit</b>, usu. c. <span class=\"lex-gram\">part.</span>, <span class=\"gk\">καὶ αὐτῇ περ νοεούσῃ</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1.577</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">καὶ ἀχνύμενός περ ἑταίρου</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">8.125</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">καὶ πρίν περ θυμῷ μεμαώς</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">5.135</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">καὶ κήδεά περ πεπαθυίῃ</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Od.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">17.555</span> </span>: so in later Poets, <span class=\"gk\">κ. ἀχνύμενος</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pi.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">I.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">8(7).4</span> </span>, cf. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">N.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">6.6</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">καὶ θοῦρός περ ὤν</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">A.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Fr.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">199.2</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">κ. αὐθάδη φρονῶν</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Id.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Pr.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">907</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">κ. οὐ στέργων ὅμως</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Id.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Th.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">712</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">κ. οὐ δύσοργος ὤν</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">S.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Ph.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">377</span> </span>: preceded by <span class=\"gk\">ὅμως</span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pl.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">R.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">495d</span> </span>: the <span class=\"lex-gram\">part.</span> must freq. be supplied, <span class=\"gk\">καὶ θεός περ</span> [<span class=\"gk\">ὤν</span>] <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">A.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Ag.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1203</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">γιγνώσκω σαφῶς, κ. σκοτεινὸς</span> [<span class=\"gk\">ὤν</span>], <span class=\"gk\">τήν γε σὴν αὐδὴν ὅμως</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">S.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">OT</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1326</span> </span>; also <span class=\"gk\">εἰ μέμονάς γε, καὶ ὀψέ περ</span> [<span class=\"gk\">ἐρυόμενος</span>],.. <span class=\"gk\">ἐρύεσθαι</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Il.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">9.247</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">ἐπιμνησαίμεθα Χάρμης, καὶ πρὸς δαίμονά περ</span> [<span class=\"gk\">μαχούμενοι</span>] <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">17.104</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">λέγεις ἀληθῆ, κ. ἐκ μακροῦ Χρόνου</span> [<span class=\"gk\">λέγων</span>] <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">S.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">OT</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1141</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">ἀλλ' ἔστιν ὧν δεῖ, κ. οὐ πολλῶν ἄπο,</span> = καίπερ οὐ πολλῶν ὄντων, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Id.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Ph.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">647</span> </span>: with finite Verbs only as dub. l., <span class=\"gk\">κ. ἔχει</span> (leg. <span class=\"gk\">καἴπερ</span>) <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pi.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">N.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">4.36</span> </span>; <span class=\"lex-itype gk\">κ</span>. (leg. <span class=\"gk\">καίτοι</span>) <span class=\"gk\"> ἐκεῖνό γε ᾤμην τι εἶναι</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pl.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Smp.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">219c</span> </span>.</div></div>"}